!scope=row|{{sortname|Alfie|Conn, Jr.}}
|align="left"|{{fba|SCO}}||MF||1976–1979||37 ||8||<ref group = "note">[[Alfie Conn, Jr.|Alfie Conn]] became the first post-war footballer to play for both [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] and Celtic. He was also the first player to ever win [[Scottish Cup]] medals with both Old Firm clubs.</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=McLeod|first=Keith|title=Alfie Still Delivers in the Box|url=http://www.dailyrecord.co.uk/news/uk-world-news/alfie-still-delivers-in-the-box-967577|accessdate=9 September 2015|work=Daily Record|date=30 January 2008}}</ref><ref>{{cite book|last=Gordon|first=Alex|title=Celtic: The Awakening: From East End Misfits to European Masters|date=2013|publisher=Mainstream Publishing|isbn=978-1-78057-635-0|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=qUSyTSShqn4C&q=alfie+conn+first+player+cup+medals+old+firm&pg=PT322}}</ref>
